message: "If you use this project, please cite the repository using this metadata."
title: "SILICON: Pre-Silicon Response Predictability in an Open-Flow Ring-Oscillator PUF"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Demetrashvili
    given-names: Nikoloz
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikodemetrashvili2010-bit/tt-ro-puf"
url: "https://github.com/nikodemetrashvili2010-bit/tt-ro-puf"
abstract: >-
  Open SKY130 pre-silicon study of how much of a ring-oscillator PUF response
  is fixed by the automated layout and therefore readable from the public
  design database, with a matched-macro comparison arm on the same die and a
  planned multi-chip validation protocol.
keywords:
  - ring oscillator
  - physical unclonable function
  - SKY130
  - OpenLane
  - OpenROAD
  - post-layout simulation
  - hardware security
  - response predictability
